hypotheses.statement:
Let $k\ge2$, $b\in A_+$, and let $a\in\mathop{\mathrm{Ideal}}_A(b)$ be a positive contraction. Suppose that, for some finite $C>0$, $$\label{loc:relative-rank}
 d_\tau(a)\le C d_\tau(b)\qquad\text{for every }\tau.$$ There is a c.p.c. order-zero map $\phi:M_k\to A_\omega\cap A'$ with weight $h$ such that every positive contractive representative $(h_n)$ of $h$ has the following property: for every $\eta>0$, on a common $\omega$-large set of coordinates, $$\label{loc:TL}
 \tau\bigl(a^{1/2}(1-h_n)a^{1/2}\bigr)
       \le\eta d_\tau(b)
 \qquad(d_\tau(b)<\infty).$$ In particular the left side is exactly zero when $d_\tau(b)=0$.

outputs.exact_statement:
There is a numerical constant $0<c<1$ with the following property for every $C^*$-algebra $A$ satisfying <span class="upright">(C)</span>. If $a,b\in A$ are positive contractions and $z\in\widetilde A$ satisfies $\|p_a z p_b\|\le1$, there are positive contractions $a'\in\mathop{\mathrm{her}}(a)$ and $b'\in\mathop{\mathrm{her}}(b)$ such that $$\label{shr:conclusion}
 \|p_{a'}z p_{b'}\|\le c$$ and, for every irreducible representation $\sigma$ of $A$, $$\label{shr:visibility}
 \max\{\|\sigma(a)\|,\|\sigma(b)\|\}\ge\tfrac12
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \sigma(a')\ne0\ \text{or}\ \sigma(b')\ne0.$$ The support norms are computed in the bidual, or equivalently in the universal representation.

Assume that $A$ satisfies <span class="upright">(C)</span>. Suppose that positive contractions $s_1,\ldots,s_m\in A$ have nonvanishing loci covering $\mathcal K(x,\gamma)$. For each pair $i\ne j$, prescribe a finite set $\mathcal E_{ij}\subset\widetilde A$, and let $\delta>0$. There are positive contractions $t_i\in\mathop{\mathrm{her}}(s_i)$, with supports $Q_i=p_{t_i}$, such that $$\begin{aligned}
 \max_i\|\sigma(t_i)\|&=1
                 &&(\sigma\in\mathcal K(x,\gamma)),       \label{norm:retained-cover}\\
 \|Q_i z Q_j\|&\le\delta
                 &&(i\ne j,\ z\in\mathcal E_{ij}).        \label{norm:cross-compressions}
\end{aligned}$$

Fix $k\geq2$ and put $$L=(20k)^2,\qquad C_k=1+4L.$$ Let $F\subset D$ be a finite set of selfadjoint contractions, let $\mathcal P\subseteq F$ consist of positive contractions, and let $0<\delta<1$. For every $\varepsilon>0$ there is a c.p.c. order-zero map $V:M_k\to D$ such that, for every $\tau\in T_{\leq1}(D)$, $$\begin{aligned}
 \sup_{\|x\|\leq1}\|[a,V(x)]\|_{2,\tau}
 &<\varepsilon &&(a\in F),\label{tr:central-target}\\
 \tau(aV(1))
 &\geq \frac\delta3\tau(a)-C_k\delta^{3/2}-\varepsilon
 &&(a\in\mathcal P).\label{tr:mass-target}
\end{aligned}$$ In particular, $k$ is fixed before the accuracy is chosen; no bound on the number of nuclear approximation summands is required.

Let $B$ be a $C^*$-algebra, and let $\phi_1,\phi_2:M_k\to B$ be c.p.c. order-zero maps with commuting ranges. Set $h_i=\phi_i(1)$. There is a c.p.c. order-zero map $\phi:M_k\to
C^*(\phi_1(M_k),\phi_2(M_k))$ such that $$\label{loc:join-weight}
 \phi(1)=1-(1-h_1)(1-h_2)=h_1+h_2-h_1h_2.$$ Its weight dominates both $h_1$ and $h_2$. If both original maps commute with a subset of an ambient algebra, the joined map also commutes with that subset.

Let $k\ge2$, $b\in A_+$, and let $a\in\mathop{\mathrm{Ideal}}_A(b)$ be a positive contraction. Suppose that, for some finite $C>0$, $$\label{loc:relative-rank}
 d_\tau(a)\le C d_\tau(b)\qquad\text{for every }\tau.$$ There is a c.p.c. order-zero map $\phi:M_k\to A_\omega\cap A'$ with weight $h$ such that every positive contractive representative $(h_n)$ of $h$ has the following property: for every $\eta>0$, on a common $\omega$-large set of coordinates, $$\label{loc:TL}
 \tau\bigl(a^{1/2}(1-h_n)a^{1/2}\bigr)
       \le\eta d_\tau(b)
 \qquad(d_\tau(b)<\infty).$$ In particular the left side is exactly zero when $d_\tau(b)=0$.*


*The finite-coordinate form permits arbitrary relative trace accuracies together with prescribed finite norm tests. Given a finite set $F\subset A$, finitely many pairs $(a_l,b_l)$ satisfying <a href="#loc:relative-rank" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="loc:relative-rank">[loc:relative-rank]</a> with finite constants $C_l$, positive accuracies $\eta_l$, and $\rho>0$, there is a c.p.c. map $\theta:M_k\to A$ whose matrix-unit order-zero defects and commutators with $F$ have norm less than $\rho$, and whose weight satisfies $$\label{loc:TL-coordinate}
 \tau\bigl(a_l^{1/2}(1-\theta(1))a_l^{1/2}\bigr)
     \le\eta_l d_\tau(b_l)
 \qquad(d_\tau(b_l)<\infty)$$ for every $l$, simultaneously over all the indicated traces.

For every fixed $k\ge2$ there is a c.p.c. order-zero map $\zeta^k:M_k\to A_\omega\cap A'$ with weight $H$ such that, for every test $(a,\varepsilon)$, if $$\label{cmp:u-y}
 u^k(a)=(1-f(H))a,
 \qquad y^k(a)=g(\zeta^k)(e_{11})^2a,$$ there is $r_{a,\varepsilon}^k\in A_\omega$ satisfying $$\label{cmp:bounded-comparison}
 (u^k(a)-\varepsilon)_+
   =(r_{a,\varepsilon}^k)^*y^k(a)r_{a,\varepsilon}^k,
 \qquad \|r_{a,\varepsilon}^k\|^2\le32/\varepsilon.$$ In particular the witness bound is independent of $k$.

For every $p\ge2$ there are a c.p.c. order-zero map $\alpha:M_p\to A_\omega\cap A'$, with weight $h=\alpha(1)$, and contractions $s_j\in A_\omega\cap A'$ for $j\ge1$ such that, putting $P=s_1$, one has $$\label{cmp:slot-relations}
 P\ge0,\qquad s_i^*s_j=\delta_{ij}P^2,
 \qquad \alpha(e_{11})s_j=s_j.$$ For every test $(a,\varepsilon)$ there is $r_{a,\varepsilon}\in A_\omega$ with $$\label{cmp:slot-comparison}
 ((1-h)a-\varepsilon)_+
       =r_{a,\varepsilon}^*(P^2a)r_{a,\varepsilon},
 \qquad \|r_{a,\varepsilon}\|^2\le64/\varepsilon.$$ No centrality is asserted or needed for these comparison witnesses.

Let $A$ be a separable $C^*$-algebra, and suppose there is a unital homomorphism $\varphi:\mathcal Z\to F_\omega(A)$. For finite sets $F\subset A$, $G\subset A\otimes\mathcal Z$, and $\varepsilon>0$, there is a unitary $u\in A^{\sim}\otimes\mathcal Z$ such that $$\label{abs:unitary-criterion}
 \|[u,a\otimes1]\|<\varepsilon\quad(a\in F),\qquad
 \mathop{\mathrm{dist}}(u^*bu,A\otimes1)<\varepsilon\quad(b\in G).$$
